      "title": {
        "en": "Welcoming and attentive boarding attendants"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Clients frequently highlight the warmth, diligence, and helpfulness of the team at Pet Paradise. Owners appreciate that staff members remember pets by name, assist with check-in smoothly, and show genuine affection toward boarding dogs and daycare attendees."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 16,
      "title": {
        "en": "Engaging play sessions for dogs"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Reviewers emphasize how energetic and happy their dogs are after group playtimes, pool sessions, and exercise yards. Many pet parents note that even shy or senior dogs are handled with patience, returning home calm, well-exercised, and eager to revisit the resort."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "place",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 11,
      "title": {
        "en": "Clean facility near Hobby Airport"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet owners consistently praise the cleanliness of the suites and the supreme convenience of the facility's location right next to William P. Hobby Airport. The dog pool, organized play yards, and tidy boarding quarters provide reassurance to travelers."
      }
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Where is the resort located relative to Hobby Airport?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Pet Paradise is located just minutes from William P. Hobby Airport, making drop-off and pickup very convenient for traveling pet parents."
      },
      "basis": "reviews"
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Are webcams available to check on pets?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Certain boarding suites offer live webcam feeds, though reviewers note that outdoor play yard camera views may be limited at times."
      },
      "basis": "reviews"
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Does the facility offer water play for dogs?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Yes, the resort features a bone-shaped swimming pool where staff supervise dogs during group and individual water play sessions."
      },
      "basis": "both"
    }
